// SW5, the endgame pool (plans/ending-spec.html section 9): said only after you choose to stay. Every line is
// gated by the bare condition "endgame" (EN2 adds it to the line filter, section 22); "endgame:early" marks the
// lines that only make sense in the first two weeks after you stay (RV21).

== chat
? endgame:early
- You stayed! Good. The best window on Deck 5 this week is yours. I've decided.   #warm
? endgame:early
- I sang at the window seat this morning. On purpose. Short version of why: you.   #funny
? endgame
- Ordinary shift. Coils, overlook, a cold tea by the glass. Sounds dull. It isn't.
- The stars look the same from here as before. Somehow better. That's a technical term.   #funny
- Bright side of staying: the dawn chorus keeps its audience. Dry side: the dawn chorus.   #funny

== bye
? endgame
- Bye! Find a window. There's always a good one.
